# GCC's libgomp does not publish an OpenMP team join to ThreadSanitizer.
# searchRings and RingUpdater::fastEnumerate read a RingPool's ring count
# on the calling thread only after the team has returned. The worker that
# enumerated that source wrote the count. The one-thread and several-thread
# ring lists compare equal, so the join does order the two accesses. Each
# source has its own pool; the counters are not shared.
race:searchRings
race:fastEnumerate
